      "draft": true,
      "body": "This draft adds Cortex runtime identity and scoped grants, governed domain access, and per-operation model admission/accounting. Gateway dispatch records immutable terminal evidence before checking current authority for private result attachment. Unsupported money remains UNKNOWN with its reservation retained and STOP enforced. Current-source production qualification is EMPTY.\n\nOffline validation passed fresh independent policy and Gateway reviews (4.4/5): 133 original and 57 new policy tests, 160 current Gateway tests, 78 historical assertions and 14 independent groups. Four affected catalog-test updates passed review and 454 tests. Root lint passed with zero errors/115 warnings; SDK build and packed ESM/CJS, declarations and browser contracts passed. The broader unit run passed 5,772 tests and retained seven attachment upload/file-URL failures.\n\nThe qualification harness is still being repaired. Independent source and parent reviews found a durability defect in existing-ID custody acknowledgement. A preparation helper also modified a protected derived namespace; exact bytes were recovered and independently checked, but historical custody continuity remains broken. Accepted lossless evidence transport and nofollow content restoration support inspection of the preserved packets; they do not certify runtime qualification. Older packets require their recorded materializers, so there is no aggregate clean-checkout claim for all historical evidence.\n\nThe launcher component passed 81 controls and independent review. Full C3 composition was rejected after a restoration failure masked the primary error. C4 added a fixed approval-gated launcher, exhaustive cleanup and generated-input recording; all six affected control commands passed. Fresh C4 review found consumed generated metadata and historical reads outside the captured closure, so original execution remains blocked. The frozen candidates, failures, reviews and authenticated content backing are preserved; C5 repaired metadata/historical input capture and passed fresh external-launcher, custody, cleanup and ROOT-surrogate controls. Fresh full C5 review rejected it (3.0/5): the VM wrapper rejects a valid original optional-identifier call, generated in-memory parent strings lack exact recipe validation and before-consumer capture, whole historical-route timing is unproved, and fault-path coverage is incomplete. C6 implementation is underway in a separate namespace, preserving all original assertions and limits. A frozen independent writer-role source aid and ROOT verification preserve the observed metadata output mapping; they do not award composition acceptance. All 122 original qualification commands remain HELD. Task 05 source preparation is accepted; dependent text-runtime implementation remains held by Task 04 and foundation gates. The conditional compiler-tier design is not adopted, and current-source native completion within the original 20-minute bound is unproved.\n\nThe last completed checkpoint's PR CI passed package/browser contracts, Neo4j/Memgraph contracts, four demo builds and basic-template unit tests. SDK/CLI/provider/lint-typecheck/deployment jobs and other demo unit steps were skipped. Signature verification failed; the checkpoint 40 CodeQL analysis was cancelled. Actual OpenAPI audit and supply-chain scanning were skipped. The current evidence checkpoint's PR/security CI is pending. Full-core, live inference, managed recall, authenticated text flows, remaining scoped capabilities and affected UI coverage are incomplete. Billing provenance, browser and signing access remain pending.\n\nEvidence, failures, task progress and actual receipts are under `_goals/convex-backend-runtime-2026-10-02/qa/`. Approved scope is in `implementation-prompt.md`; settled decisions are in `_research/convex-ai-gateway-2026-10-02/decision-gates.md`. No merge, production deployment or package publication.",
